 ## Background
 
-Delta tracking, also known as Woodcock tracking, was initially developed in the 1950s and 1960s by Butcher and Messel (1958, 1960), Zerby et al. (1961), Bertini (1963), Woodcock et al. (1965), Miller (1967), and Coleman (1968) [S16, unofficial]. It was originally designed for neutron transport simulations in heterogeneous media [S16, unofficial]. In computer graphics, it has been adopted for unbiased volumetric path tracing to handle complex participating media without the bias of ray marching [S14][S12, unofficial]. It is implemented in systems like OSPRay using ISPC and exposed via the Open VKL API for volume rendering of RBF particle data [S2, book].
